div.p:
In our own councils there are a variety and a composite of issues: There are
                    issues between principles and opportunism; between confindence and fear; between
                    reality and illusion; between clear understanding and confused misunderstanding;
                    between wisdom and folly; between being farsighted and being shortsighted;
                    between the concept 
 of peace at any
                    price and a concept of peace at a price commensurate with the value of peace;
                    between accurate appraisal and inaccurate appraisal of our own strength; between
                    full use and fractional use of our material and moral resources.
